        "definition": "Objective, Goals, Strategies, Measures. A one-page strategic planning framework used by P&G, Coca-Cola, and Mars. Bridges vision (Objective) to execution (Measures) with clear accountability.",
        "example": "Objective (qualitative, inspiring): 'Be the #1 healthy snack brand in US schools.' | Goals (quantitative, time-bound): 20% market share by 2027, $500M revenue, available in 10,000 schools. | Strategies (how to achieve goals): Partner with school districts (#1), launch kid-friendly packaging (#2), influencer marketing campaign (#3). | Measures (KPIs per strategy): # school district contracts signed, product placement in vending machines, social media impressions. | Entire OGSM fits on one page. Every employee can see how their work connects to company objectives.",
