    "name": "Porter's Five Forces",
    "definition": "Analyzes industry competitiveness through five forces",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Airlines: High rivalry (many competitors), high buyer power (price comparison), high supplier power (Boeing/Airbus duopoly), medium substitutes (trains, video calls), low barriers (anyone can lease planes). Result: terrible industry returns. | Soft drinks (Coke/Pepsi): Low rivalry (duopoly), low buyer power (brand loyalty), low supplier power (commodity ingredients), low substitutes, HIGH barriers (distribution network, brand). Result: 30%+ ROIC. | Streaming (Netflix): Rivalry rising (Disney+, HBO, Apple). Supplier power rising (content costs). Substitutes: YouTube, gaming. Barriers dropping.",
