    "name": "Stage-Gate Process",
    "definition": "Structured innovation funnel: Ideas enter, pass through gates (go/kill decisions) at each stage. Reduces risk by killing bad ideas early before heavy investment.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Stages: Discovery (idea generation) → Gate 1: Is it aligned with strategy? → Scoping (quick assessment) → Gate 2: Does market exist? → Business Case (detailed analysis) → Gate 3: Is ROI sufficient? → Development → Gate 4: Is product ready? → Testing/Validation → Gate 5: Launch ready? → Launch. | Pharmaceutical: ~10,000 compounds → 250 pre-clinical → 5 clinical trials → 1 approved drug. Stage-Gate kills 99.99% before heavy costs. | Gates are decisions: Go (fund next stage), Kill (stop), Hold (wait for more data), Recycle (revise and resubmit).",
