    "name": "Porter's Generic Strategies",
    "definition": "Three fundamental competitive positions: Cost Leadership (lowest cost in industry), Differentiation (unique value customers pay premium for), and Focus (serve a narrow segment extremely well). Being 'stuck in the middle' is the worst position.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Cost Leadership: Walmart. Massive scale, efficient supply chain, lean operations. Every decision optimizes for lower cost. | Differentiation: Apple. Design, ecosystem, brand, user experience. Premium pricing (40%+ gross margin). Not the cheapest, but customers pay more willingly. | Focus: Ferrari (focused differentiation — luxury sports cars). Southwest Airlines (focused cost leadership — point-to-point, single aircraft type, no frills domestic). | Stuck in the middle: Sears. Not as cheap as Walmart, not as nice as Target. Failed both ways.",
    "tags": [
      "strategy",
      "competitive-positioning"
    ],
