    "definition": "Data-driven methodology to eliminate defects and reduce variation. DMAIC: Define (problem), Measure (current performance), Analyze (root causes), Improve (implement solutions), Control (sustain gains). Goal: 3.4 defects per million.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Define: What is the problem? (ER wait times too long). Measure: How bad is it? (Average 287 min). Analyze: Why? Root cause = lab turnaround is 42% of wait. Improve: What fixes it? Dedicated ER lab tech, 15-min SLA. Control: How do we sustain? Daily dashboard, alert at 20 min. Result: wait time 287→126 min.",
