    "name": "Lean Manufacturing / TPS",
    "definition": "Toyota Production System: Eliminate all waste (muda) — overproduction, waiting, transport, over-processing, inventory, motion, defects. Produce exactly what's needed, when needed, in the amount needed.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Toyota: Just-in-Time production — parts arrive exactly when needed, not before (reduces inventory waste). Jidoka — machines stop automatically when a defect is detected (prevents defect propagation). Kaizen — every worker can stop the line and suggest improvements (600,000 improvement suggestions/year). | 7 wastes (TIMWOOD): Transport, Inventory, Motion, Waiting, Overproduction, Over-processing, Defects. | Lean in software: Continuous deployment (reduce WIP), automated testing (reduce defect waste), pair programming (reduce waiting).",
