    "id": "",
    "name": "Hoshin Kanri / Policy Deployment",
    "definition": "Japanese strategic planning process that aligns company-wide objectives (what) with daily management (how). Cascading goals from CEO to front line with catchball (two-way negotiation) at each level.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "CEO: 'Improve quality 50% this year' (hoshin). VP Engineering interprets: 'Reduce defect rate from 2% to 1%.' Director: 'Implement automated testing for top 10 defect types.' Team lead: 'Write test suite for Module X, target 0.5% defect rate.' | Catchball: The team lead pushes back: 'Need 2 more weeks for Module X, but can deliver Module Y earlier.' The negotiation goes back up the chain. | Hoshin Review: Monthly reviews using A3 reports (one-page problem-solving documents). Green (on track), Yellow (at risk), Red (off track — needs escalation).",
