    "name": "Statistical Process Control",
    "definition": "Monitor process performance with control charts. Upper and lower control limits (typically ±3 sigma). Points outside limits = special cause (investigate). Points within limits = common cause (process is stable).",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Manufacturing: part diameter measured hourly. UCL = 10.2mm, LCL = 9.8mm. Reading at 11am: 10.5mm — outside UCL. Investigate: machine calibration drifted. Fix before producing defects. | Call center: average handle time chart. Sudden spike at 2pm — special cause (system outage). Don't retrain agents — fix the outage. | Rule of 7: seven consecutive points on one side of the mean (even within limits) also signals a process shift. Statistical, not random.",
