    "name": "After-Action Review (AAR) for War Games",
    "definition": "After every war game round, capture: 1) What did the red team exploit? 2) What surprised the blue team? 3) What assumption did blue team hold that red team disproved? 4) What's the action plan for each vulnerability found?",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "AAR template: 'Red Team successfully exploited our single-source supplier dependency.' Action: diversify suppliers, build 30-day inventory buffer. | 'Blue Team was surprised that Red Team could rally regulatory opposition.' Action: hire government relations lead, pre-brief regulators on launch. | 'Assumption disproven: we assumed competitor can't match our price point. Red Team showed they can cross-subsidize from their cash-cow product for 18 months.' Action: adjust pricing strategy accordingly.",
