    "id": "",
    "name": "Chaos Engineering",
    "definition": "Deliberately inject failures into production to verify the system handles them gracefully. 'What happens if the payment processor goes down?' Test it — don't wait for it to happen at 3am.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Netflix Chaos Monkey: randomly terminates production instances during business hours. Engineers build resilient systems because they KNOW Chaos Monkey is watching. | Game day: simulate a full database outage. Can the team recover within SLO? Runbook works in theory — does it work when you're panicking at 11pm? | Start small: kill one non-critical service. Observe. Expand to critical paths. Chaos engineering reveals assumptions: 'we thought the failover was automatic — it required manual DNS change.'",
