    "name": "Code & Architecture Quality Assessment",
    "definition": "Quick signals of codebase health: test coverage, static analysis findings, dependency freshness, architecture documentation existence, and deployment frequency. These are leading indicators of future engineering velocity.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Red flags: test coverage <20% (every change risks breaking things), dependencies >2 years out of date (security + compatibility risk), no architecture diagrams exist (tribal knowledge only), deploy frequency <1/week (slow feedback loops). | Green flags: >60% test coverage on critical paths, automated deploy pipeline, architecture decision records (ADRs) for major choices, static analysis passing in CI. | CEO question: 'If the entire engineering team quit tomorrow, could a new team understand and maintain this system in 3 months?' The answer reveals documentation and architecture quality.",
