    "name": "Engineering Team Assessment",
    "definition": "Bus factor: how many key people could get 'hit by a bus' before the system becomes unmaintainable? 1-2 people = extreme risk. Tenure distribution: if 50%+ of engineers have <1 year tenure, institutional knowledge is fragile.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Bus factor assessment: 'Who knows the payment system?' Answer: 'Just Alex.' Bus factor = 1. Risk: Alex leaves, payment system has zero experts. Mitigation: pair programming, documentation, rotation. | Tenure: 80% of engineers hired in last 12 months. Red flag: nobody remembers WHY architectural decisions were made. Cargo cult engineering. | Hiring velocity: how long to fill an open role? >3 months = talent bottleneck. High attrition among senior engineers = cultural or technical problems driving them away.",
