    "name": "Tech Debt Audit",
    "definition": "Quantify tech debt not as 'we have tech debt' (everyone does) but as a PERCENTAGE of engineering capacity consumed by maintenance vs new features. >30% maintenance capacity = tech debt crisis requiring dedicated paydown.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Survey engineers: 'What % of your time in the last quarter was spent on: bug fixes, refactoring, keeping the lights on vs new features?' Results: 45% maintenance = tech debt consuming almost half your engineering capacity. That's a $450k/quarter tax on a 10-person team. | Tech debt balance sheet: 'To reach 80% feature capacity, we need to invest 3 person-months in test coverage, 2 months in CI/CD, 1 month in monitoring.' Cost: $100k. ROI: 20% more feature output ongoing. | Payback period: $100k investment / $90k/month additional feature capacity = 1.1 month payback. Board-ready math.",
