    "name": "GDPR/CCPA Compliance Engineering",
    "definition": "Data privacy regulations require engineering changes: data inventory (what data do you have?), data subject access requests (give users their data), right to deletion (purge user data everywhere), consent management.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "GDPR DSAR: user emails 'send me all my data.' You have 30 days. Engineering challenge: user data scattered across 12 services, 3 databases, 2 data warehouses. Without a data inventory, this takes weeks. With one, it's automated. | Right to deletion: user says 'delete my data.' You must purge from primary DB, backups, analytics warehouse, and logs. Hard-delete from everywhere. Engineering must support this. | Fine risk: GDPR fines up to 4% of global revenue. For a $50M company, that's $2M. Data compliance engineering costs $200k/year. ROI = 10x risk reduction.",
