    "name": "AI Governance & Responsible AI",
    "definition": "Framework for ensuring AI is safe, fair, and compliant: bias testing, explainability, human-in-the-loop for high-stakes decisions, model cards for transparency, and alignment with emerging regulations (EU AI Act).",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Bias testing: your hiring model scores male candidates 15% higher on average. Why? Training data reflects historical hiring patterns (biased). Debiasing required before deployment. | Explainability: bank denies loan. Customer asks 'why?' If your model can't explain the decision (it's a black box), you may be violating fair lending laws. Use explainable models or SHAP/LIME for post-hoc explanations. | Human-in-the-loop: AI flags fraudulent transactions. Below $500 = auto-block. Over $500 = human reviews before blocking. Thresholds calibrated to false positive rate. | EU AI Act (2025+): high-risk AI (hiring, credit, healthcare) requires conformity assessment, human oversight, transparency. Budget $200k-500k for compliance.",
