    "name": "SOC2 / ISO 27001 Compliance",
    "definition": "SOC2 (US): proves you have controls for security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy. ISO 27001 (international): information security management system. Both require 6-12 months of preparation and are audited annually.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "SOC2 Type I: point-in-time assessment. 'As of June 1, were controls in place?' Quicker, cheaper ($30-80k). | SOC2 Type II: assessment over a period (typically 6-12 months). 'Were controls operating effectively from Jan-June?' More rigorous, enterprise customers demand this. ($50-150k). | Timeline: 3 months to design and implement controls → 1 month of evidence collection → 2 months of audit → report issued at month 6. | CEO decision: pursue SOC2 when enterprise customers >20% of pipeline AND you're losing deals to 'security review' delays. Not before — premature compliance is expensive overhead.",
