    "name": "Equity Grant Design",
    "definition": "Standard terms: 4-year vesting, 1-year cliff (no equity until 12 months). Post-termination exercise window: 90 days (standard, forces exercise or forfeiture) vs 10 years (emerging best practice, kinder to employees). Refresh grants at promotion and periodically.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "New hire grant: 40,000 options over 4 years (1-year cliff). Year 1: 0 shares vest until month 12. Then 10,000 shares vest, 2,083/month thereafter. | 90-day exercise window: employee leaves, has 90 days to exercise vested options. If not exercised, forfeited. Problem: buyer needs cash (strike price + taxes). At a unicorn, could be $500k+. Employee can't afford it, forfeits years of equity. | Extended window (10 years): gives employees time to exercise when the company is liquid. Becoming standard at progressive companies. Costs the company zero, retains employee goodwill.",
