    "name": "Regulatory Landscape Mapping",
    "definition": "Create a matrix: rows = regulations (GDPR, CCPA, SOC2, SOX, HIPAA, EU AI Act), columns = applicability (yes/no), risk level (high/med/low), compliance status (compliant/gap/unknown), and remediation cost. Prioritize by risk level.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "SaaS company with EU customers and AI features: GDPR applies (high risk, fine up to 4% global revenue), SOC2 applies (medium risk, customer requirement), EU AI Act applies (medium risk, emerging), SOX applies post-IPO (low risk now, high risk later). | Plan: Q1: close GDPR gaps (data inventory, DSAR process). Q2: SOC2 Type I. Q3: EU AI Act readiness assessment. H2: SOX prep. | Every regulation has a 'trigger event.' GDPR triggers when you have ANY EU customer. SOX triggers at IPO. Don't build compliance for regulations that don't apply yet (waste) — but know when they WILL apply.",
