    "id": "",
    "name": "Risk Transfer Spectrum",
    "definition": "Not all risks need insurance. Decision framework: 1) Can we RETAIN this risk? (low severity, predictable) 2) Can we MITIGATE it? (reduce probability or impact) 3) Can we CONTRACTUALLY transfer it? (indemnification from partners) 4) Should we INSURE it? (catastrophic, unpredictable) 5) Should we HEDGE it? (financial market risks).",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "Risk: office laptop theft. Frequency: 5/year. Severity: $2k each. Total: $10k/year. Retain — self-insure. Premium would be $15k (insurer adds admin + profit). | Risk: class action lawsuit. Severity: $50M+. Insure (D&O/E&O). Can't retain this. | Risk: FX exposure on €5M revenue. Hedge with forward contracts. Cheaper and more direct than insurance. | Risk: supplier failure. Contractual transfer: require supplier to carry business interruption insurance naming you as beneficiary. Don't insure their failure yourself.",
    "tags": [
      "risk",
      "insurance"
    ],
