    "name": "Sanctions & Export Controls",
    "definition": "US sanctions (OFAC), EU sanctions, UN sanctions — different lists, different rules. Know which apply to you based on: 1) Your jurisdiction 2) Your customers' locations 3) Your products (dual-use technology needs export license). Violating sanctions is criminal, not civil. Penalties can include prison for executives.",
    "formula": null,
    "example": "OFAC SDN list: you cannot transact with Specially Designated Nationals. This includes entities owned 50%+ by an SDN (even if the entity itself isn't on the list). | Export controls: selling encryption software to certain countries requires BIS license. Your SaaS product may be 'exported' when a user in a sanctioned country downloads it. Geolocation blocking is not optional — it's mandatory. | M&A red flag: acquired a company with customers in Iran (sanctions violation). You inherit the liability. Always include sanctions screening in M&A diligence.",
